From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: describe firmware LVDS output

KWin/PowerDevil associates internal backlights only with internal outputs.
The Unknown simpledrm connector on SM-T531 leaves its working LP8556 PWM
backlight unmatched and enables software brightness, adding an expensive
full-screen rendering pass on Adreno 305.

Describe the verified LVDS transport behind the board's TC358764 bridge.
Use a local binding extension until native DRM panel topology is complete;
this does not claim an exact LCD module or initialize any bridge/MDP block.
Unknown remains the default for existing firmware framebuffers.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
index 6d29a00bd..8d2d0d03d 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -89,6 +89,8 @@ &modem {
 };
 
 &framebuffer0 {
+	/* Firmware drives the internal LCD through TC358764 DSI-to-LVDS. */
+	connector-type = "lvds";
 	backlight = <&lcd_backlight>;
 	clocks = <&mmcc MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
 		 <&mmcc MDSS_AXI_CLK>,
